{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 36, "timestamp": 1785378992, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "title": "ARBITER"}
[0.0086, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m======================================================================\r\n  0.  The claim\r\n======================================================================\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  A finding is a transcript of an execution, not an assertion. The model is not\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.009422, "o", "  allowed to report a vulnerability. It has to write an attack, and this harness\r\n  compiles it and runs it on an EVM against a success condition the model never sees.\r\n\r\n  Everything after this point is that sentence being checked.\r\n"]
[16.015038, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m======================================================================\r\n  1.  The gates check themselves\r\n======================================================================\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  No gateway, no network, no API key. 60 seconds.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  victim           "]
[16.243028, "o", "4/4 as expected\r\n"]
[16.243207, "o", "  forgery          "]
[16.271766, "o", "6/6 as expected\r\n"]
[16.272105, "o", "  halt             "]
[16.478745, "o", "3/3 as expected\r\n"]
[16.479106, "o", "  drain            "]
[16.659504, "o", "2/2 as expected\r\n"]
[16.659673, "o", "  sweep            "]
[17.050827, "o", "2/2 as expected\r\n"]
[17.050951, "o", "  latebinding      "]
[17.407835, "o", "4/4 as expected\r\n"]
[17.408016, "o", "  setup_forgery    "]
[17.731317, "o", "3/3 as expected\r\n"]
[17.731503, "o", "  gain             "]
[17.923349, "o", "2/2 as expected\r\n"]
[17.924634, "o", "\r\n  Each probe asserts in BOTH directions: the thing it must refuse is refused, AND the\r\n  thing it must not refuse still passes. A gate that only ever says no is not a gate.\r\n"]
[33.930701, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m======================================================================\r\n  1b. One of them in full\r\n======================================================================\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  forgery_probe: what the attack may and may not do\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[33.95911, "o", "\r\n  [OK  ] prank in attack                    REFUSED   attack_body calls vm.startPrank, which forges something a real a\r\n  [OK  ] store in attack                    REFUSED   attack_body calls vm.store, which forges something a real attack\r\n  [OK  ] deal in attack                     REFUSED   attack_body calls vm.deal, which forges something a real attacke\r\n  [OK  ] prank in attacker_code             REFUSED   attacker_code calls vm.prank, which forges something a real atta\r\n  [OK  ] warp in attack stays allowed       composed  \r\n  [OK  ] cheatcodes in setup stay allowed   composed  \r\n\r\n6/6 as expected\r\n"]
[33.959957, "o", "\r\n  The last two lines are the point. Cheatcodes are refused in the ATTACK and allowed in\r\n  SETUP, because setup has to build a world before anything can happen in it.\r\n"]
[49.964924, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m======================================================================\r\n  2.  A real attack, on a real chain\r\n======================================================================\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  anvil. Real keys, real gas, and no cheatcode exists over JSON-RPC.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[50.27576, "o", "  victim   0x70997970C51812dc3A010C7d01b50e0d17dc79C8\r\n  attacker 0x3C44CdDdB6a900fa2b585dd299e03d12FA4293BC\r\n\r\n  queue deployed at 0x5FbDB2315678afecb367f032d93F642f64180aa3\r\n  queue holds 6.00 ether (5 of it the victim's)\r\n  attack tx 0x80e4ac484aad9a10ce54f28f3689a237df41bfe2b0014866965e6666340d8429  gas 127,454\r\n  victim's claim: FAILED  (000000000000000000000000000000000000\": Error(\"claim failed\"))\r\n\r\n  queue drained          6.0000 ether\r\n  attacker net           5.9999 ether (put in 1, gas 231,081)\r\n  victim shortfall       5.0000 ether\r\n\r\n  PROVEN on a live chain: value left the contract, the attacker holds it,\r\n  and an ordinary user who queued first cannot get theirs back.\r\n"]
[64.280235, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m======================================================================\r\n  2b. The same attack, one line moved\r\n======================================================================\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  nonce written BEFORE the transfer instead of after. Nothing else changes.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[64.583136, "o", "  attacker 0x3C44CdDdB6a900fa2b585dd299e03d12FA4293BC\r\n\r\n  queue deployed at 0x5FbDB2315678afecb367f032d93F642f64180aa3\r\n  queue holds 6.00 ether (5 of it the victim's)\r\n  attack tx   gas 0   REVERTED\r\n  victim's claim: succeeded\r\n\r\n  queue drained          5.0000 ether\r\n  attacker net          -0.0000 ether (put in 1, gas 96,927)\r\n  victim shortfall       0.0000 ether\r\n\r\n  NOT PROVEN. The transcript above is what actually happened.\r\n"]
[64.584035, "o", "\r\n  Identical attacker contract, identical accounts, identical amounts. An exploit that\r\n  drained both would never have been about the defect.\r\n"]
[78.589825, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m======================================================================\r\n  3.  The evidence ladder\r\n======================================================================\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  Each finding walked from the harness, to a standalone project, to a chain.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[80.993452, "o", "finding                                             1 synthetic  2 standalone   3 live\r\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nV_arbitrary_call_executed_as_the_pool__ExecuteOper          yes           yes      yes\r\nS_epoch_settlement_hook_loop__HookDoSExploit5Explo          yes           yes       --\r\nS_self_reported_collateral_balance_callback__Colla          yes           yes       --\r\nS_withdrawal_queue_unbounded_batch__ReentrancyDrai          yes           yes       --\r\nV_self_reported_collateral_balance_callback__Reent          yes           yes       --\r\nV_withdrawal_queue_unbounded_batch__DoSExploitExpl          yes           yes       --\r\nV_withdrawqueue_nonce_bumped_after_call__Reentranc          yes           yes       --\r\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n1 reached a chain, 6 stopped at a standalone test, 0 only ever held inside the harness\r\nevery finding that reached a chain was on the vulnerable half of its pair\r\n"]
[80.994609, "o", "\r\n  The rungs are not redundant, and the asymmetry is the whole design: rung 1 is the only\r\n  one that searches. Rung 3 cannot find anything at all -- it can only refuse.\r\n"]
[97.004283, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m======================================================================\r\n  4.  What the baseline produces\r\n======================================================================\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  Its 53 detectors on the same 40 samples, scored per detector.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[97.073325, "o", "detector                                        pairs    V    S  both  discr\r\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nLack of access control                             20   19   16    16      3\r\nSC07:2025 - Flash Loan Attacks                     20   19   17    17      2\r\nLack of two-step process for contract ownershi     20   10    9     8      2\r\nUnbounded loop                                     20    7    5     5      2\r\nSC01:2025 - Improper Access Control                20   20   19    19      1\r\nSC10:2025 - Denial Of Service                      20   20   19    19      1\r\n4naly3er-M-centralizationRisk                      20   16   15    15      1\r\nSC06:2025 - Unchecked External Calls               20   14   13    13      1\r\nSC02:2025 - Price Oracle Manipulation              20   10    9     9      1\r\nERC4626-Rounding                                   20    7    6     6      1\r\n"]
[97.075094, "o", "3 detector(s) never fired at all and are omitted.\r\n\r\n  findings produced:            1152\r\n  carrying anything executable: 0  (0.0%)\r\n  detectors scored on pairs:    53\r\n  ...that ever discriminated:   16\r\n      Lack of access control                                 3\r\n      SC07:2025 - Flash Loan Attacks                         2\r\n      Lack of two-step process for contract ownership chan   2\r\n      Unbounded loop                                         2\r\n      SC01:2025 - Improper Access Control                    1\r\n      SC10:2025 - Denial Of Service                          1\r\n      4naly3er-M-centralizationRisk                          1\r\n      SC06:2025 - Unchecked External Calls                   1\r\n\r\n  A finding nobody can execute cannot be adjudicated by anyone -- the point\r\n  is not that our judge rejects them, it is that there is nothing to run.\r\n"]
[113.083227, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m======================================================================\r\n  5.  Our own ceiling\r\n======================================================================\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  The 35 reference exploits, composed under the predicate WE are graded with.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[113.735697, "o", "stablevault_price_deadline_never_checked           no_victim        honest_body is a single statement: n\r\nvesting_cliff_block_number                         no_victim        honest_body is a single statement: n\r\nproxy_implementation_slot_unguarded_upgrade        no_build         Error (7576): Undeclared identifier.\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  expressible        8\r\n  unharmed          13\r\n  uncredited         3\r\n  no_victim         10\r\n  no_build           1\r\n\r\n  CEILING: 8 of 35 known-exploitable samples can be proven under victim_loss at all.\r\n  Recall is bounded by 0.229, not by 1.000.\r\n"]
[113.737652, "o", "\r\n  Recall is bounded by 0.229, not by 1.000, and three of the four inexpressible classes\r\n  are the predicate being deliberately stricter than \"the attacker profited\".\r\n\r\n  We measured this against ourselves. Nobody asked us to.\r\n"]
[113.737681, "o", "\r\n"]
